so it isn't near-unanimous. The vote falls in his current Assembly term.\n- **The provision:** Section 220.5(a) of the chaptered text says schools \"shall not enact or enforce any policy, rule, or administrative regulation that would require\" staff to disclose a pupil's gender identity without the pupil's consent. That matches rung 2 clause for clause.\n- **Why not rung 1:** Section 220.3 says staff \"shall not be required to disclose\". It doesn't forbid disclosure, so it doesn't order staff to keep the information from parents.\n- **The source tier will be single-source.** The vote page and the bill text are one record on one instrument, not two sources. There were no quotes in his own words to tier.\n\nTwo judgment calls a second coder could read differently:\n- **Preemption:** I coded the bill as on-question rather than adjacent. It forbids local rules, which the codebook usually treats as adjacent, but here forbidding those rules is what rung 2 itself says.\n- **Single subject:** I treated the bill as single-subject. Its other sections (resources for parents of LGBTQ pupils, protection for staff from retaliation) relate to the same matter. A coder who calls it multi-subject would get BLANK `direction-only` instead of rung 2.","ttft_ms":10279,"type":"result","duration_ms":28112,"uuid":"146f9899-a97f-49dd-ae43-8dab08a368d8","ttft_stream_ms":1894,"time_to_request_ms":170,"first_content_frame_ms":1894,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
